# Backend Adapter Rule (CI-enforced)

Engine code talks **only** to:

- `backends/i_speech_to_text.hpp`
- `backends/i_language_model.hpp`
- `backends/i_text_to_speech.hpp`

Mode selection: **only** `backends/loader.cpp::run_worker()`.

If you want to branch on `backend_mode` from engine code → the interface is missing an abstraction. Add it there instead.

## Extend a backend feature

1. Extend the relevant `i_*.hpp`
2. Implement in **all three** families: Local + OpenAI + Mistral
3. Emit `[STT|LM|TTS]-[LOCAL|OPENAI|MISTRAL]` on every inference call

## Audit invariants (`tests/test_audit_logging.cpp`)

| Files | Must have | Must NOT contain |
|-------|-----------|------------------|
| `whisper_stt` / `llama_lm` / `piper_tts` | `*-LOCAL` | `OPENAI`, `MISTRAL`, `api.openai.com`, `api.mistral.ai`, `curl_easy_perform` |
| `openai_*` | `*-OPENAI` | `whisper.h`, `llama.h`, `piper.h`, `-LOCAL]`, `-MISTRAL]` |
| `mistral_*` | `*-MISTRAL` | `whisper.h`, `llama.h`, `piper.h`, `-LOCAL]`, `-OPENAI]`, `api.openai.com` |

Local backend headers: `#include` only inside `#ifdef XPWELLYS_USE_LOCAL_INFERENCE` — sole consumer is `loader.cpp`. Local backends must not use libcurl.
